Bluetooth: advertising on or off (plat_ble_advertise), the advertised name from fm1.toml, and a found device's
address (plat_ble_found_addr).
- plat_ble_advertise(on): a computer may find and connect to the FM-1 (BLE-Periphery), or not; off lets a connected
  computer go and keeps the device's link (BLE-Central). ble/midi/le_midi.c keeps the wish (adv_wanted), so none of
  the places that advertise again after a link undoes it. From ignis32's tornado (its patches/fm1-base/0003).
- fm1.toml ble_name = "...": the name advertised and in the GAP name (FM1B_BLE_NAME; "FM-1" without it), 1..29
  printable ASCII characters. The advertising packet holds 8 beside the flags and the MIDI service's UUID: a longer
  name goes there shortened (type 0x08) and whole in the scan response (0x09). tornado's took 8 at most.
- plat_ble_found_addr(i, addr): the address of device i of the scan, as written (most significant byte first), for a
  list that tells devices of one name apart and for reconnecting to the one chosen. The host simulator: "ble devices
  N" (N stand-ins, C0:FF:EE:00:10:0i) and "ble lose" (the connected one goes away).
Why MIDIMON needs it: its BLUETOOTH page (BLE-P and BLE-C apart, a device list with addresses, reconnecting to the
chosen device), and the name FM1_MONITOR on Bluetooth (USB keeps "MIDIMON FM-1": the installers look for "FM-1").
Applies to: fm1-base aa2b3bc, after 0001 and 0002. Upstream: not offered yet.
